# MOONSHOTS — Next-Generation Architectural Horizons & Sovereign Moat

File: openOODA/MOONSHOTS.oot
Long-term architectural horizons, sovereign paradigm shifts, and moonshot tracks.
All future tracks align with the 6 Strategic Pillars, the 5 Evolution Phases, and the Blue Ocean moat.
Active sprint tasks, release pin (v2.5.4), and near-term deliverables live in ROADMAP.oot.

## 0. Strategic Architecture Alignment & Evolution Phases

The openOODA horizon advances through 5 evolutionary phases under Generational SemVer (`v<Floor>.<Thrust>.<Patch>`):
  - Phase 1 (Kinematic to Informational OODA): Elevating mechanical Ps optimization to AST observation and SMT contract orientation.
  - Phase 2 (Centralized to Distributed State Mesh): Multi-agent sensor fusion consensus and peer-to-peer capability verification.
  - Phase 3 (Static Code to Autonomous Swarm Adaptation): Real-time AST mutation, live PGO, and ghost-state Undo-RAM execution.
  - Phase 4 (Boundary Physics Limits): Hard mathematical bounds via Rice's theorem, CAP theorem, and Landauer's principle.
  - Phase 5 (Generational Loop Encapsulation): Encapsulating Gen 1-4 reflexes under Gen 5 swarms and Gen 6 sovereign intelligence.
  - Power Law 80/20 Weighted Floor Rule: Major Moonshot transitions advance the Generational Floor (F=3 to F=6).

---

## 1. Phase 1: Kinematic to Informational OODA & Via Negativa

[ ] Via Negativa Subtractive Drag Elimination Engine (Pillar 2 Boyd's E-M Engine)
    Systematically eliminate computational drag (D -> 0) across compiler and runtime pipelines.
    Replace dynamic heap allocation with linear arenas and O(1) bulk resets.
    Elide runtime contract checks through compile-time SMT proof generation.

[ ] Full-Spectrum AST Observation & Cryptographic Merkle Diffing (Pillar 2 Informational E-M)
    Ingest source code changes as cryptographic Merkle AST digests.
    Compress orientation latency from O(N) full scans to O(log N) subtree diffs.
    Enable sub-millisecond OODA loop turnover across agent swarms.

[ ] Automated Binary Transmutation & Telemetry Stripping (Pillar 5 Blue Ocean Moat)
    Ingest foreign legacy binaries (C/C++, Rust, Go, Zig, WASM).
    Statically trace call graphs and concolic syscall reachability.
    Strip ambient tracking, telemetry, and ungranted system access.
    Re-emit hardened native OODA binaries with explicit capability tokens.

---

## 2. Phase 2: Distributed State Mesh & Consensus Mesh

[ ] Byzantine Fault Tolerant Capability DAG Consensus (Pillar 6 Swarm Collaboration)
    Coordinate heterogeneous agent swarms over a decentralized capability DAG.
    Converge distributed sensor fusion and state transitions in O(log M) communication rounds.
    Authenticate inter-agent wire framing using Noise XX handshakes and ChaCha20-Poly1305 seals.

[ ] Peer-to-Peer SMT Proof Verification Mesh (Pillar 3 Negative Trust)
    Distribute contract verification workloads across peer agent swarms.
    Verify SMT proofs and capability grants independently before state commits.
    Prevent forged capability propagation across untrusted network nodes.

[ ] Decentralized Zero-Knowledge Verifiable Compute (Pillar 5 Sovereign Moat)
    Pair SECRET field taint tracking with cryptographic ZK-STARK execution proofs.
    Execute code on untrusted decentralized cloud nodes with mathematical proof of contract compliance.
    Protect private data without exposing secret fields to untrusted hosts.

---

## 3. Phase 3: Autonomous Swarm Adaptation & Real-Time Mutation

[ ] Real-Time AST Mutation & Live Machine Code Re-Emission (Pillar 6 Swarm Adaptation)
    Autonomous fibers detect runtime execution hotspots and hostile probing attacks.
    Mutate AST subtrees in memory (e.g. convert Array-of-Structs to Struct-of-Arrays for SIMD).
    Prove safety against SMT preconditions and re-emit ELF64/WASM bytes with zero downtime.

[ ] Live Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO) Feedback Loop (Pillar 2 E-M Thrust Acceleration)
    Feed runtime branch bias, loop trip counts, and cache telemetry back into SSA optimizer.
    Reorder basic blocks and propagate dynamic constants in running binary images.

[ ] Ghost-State Transactional Memory (Undo-RAM) (Pillar 3 Adversarial Hardening)
    Execute speculative mutations inside isolated micro-transactional memory bubbles.
    On contract violation or memory anomaly, roll back state changes instantly (O(1) pointer reset).
    Attenuate offending capabilities and commit only verified safe state transitions.

[ ] Sub-Millisecond Autonomous One-Turn Repair (Pillar 6 Multi-Agent Swarm)
    Eliminate human cognitive latency bottlenecks (10^5 ms -> <= 10^2 ms).
    Detect compile or runtime errors, synthesize AST patches, and certify fixes in one turn.

---

## 4. Phase 4: Boundary Physics & Mathematical Invariants

[ ] Rice-Bounded Decidable Contract Synthesis (Pillar 1 First Principles)
    Enforce Rice's theorem boundaries by restricting contracts to decidable First-Order Logic fragments (QF_LIA, QF_BV).
    Apply deterministic SMT solver timeouts and fail closed on unverified contracts.

[ ] Asynchronous Monotonic CAP Leases (Pillar 5 Zero Ambient Authority)
    Prioritize Consistency and Safety over Availability under network partitions.
    Enforce monotonic local capability attenuation (ChildCap subset of ParentCap).
    Expire capability leases automatically into default-deny states during communication loss.

[ ] Landauer Minimal Thermodynamic Entropy Teardowns (Pillar 1 Silicon Invariants)
    Minimize thermodynamic bit erasure entropy (Delta Q >= kB * T * ln 2).
    Structure memory in contiguous linear arenas with O(1) bulk pointer resets.
    Implement zero-leak deterministic RAII Automatic Reference Counting without garbage collection pauses.

---

## 5. Phase 5: Generational Loop Encapsulation & Sovereign Microkernel

[ ] Autonomic Reflex Stratum Encapsulation (Pillar 1 First Principles)
    Encapsulate Gen 1 (Silicon HAL), Gen 2 (Compiler IR), Gen 3 (Runtime Memory), and Gen 4 (Type System) into deterministic reflexes.
    Free Gen 5 (Multi-Agent Swarms) and Gen 6 (Sovereign Intelligence) from manual verification of base invariants.

[ ] Bare-Metal Reflexive Sovereign Microkernel (Pillar 1 Hardware Sovereignty)
    Implement bare-metal operating system kernel entirely in pure .oo.
    Directly map hardware interrupts, MMU page tables (PML4/Sv39), and device controllers to capability tokens.
    Run Gen 5 and Gen 6 sovereign swarms directly on hardware without host operating system layers.

[ ] Autonomous Intent Synthesis & Metamorphic Binaries (Pillar 6 Intent Synthesis)
    Synthesize high-level natural language intent and formal contracts into verified native machine code.
    Continuously morph binary layouts, CFI shadow stacks, and Merkle call-edge hashes to eliminate exploitation.
